   "evidence": "FY2027 $4.6M equals 360 robots at $12,778 but only 110 are contracted [S1]; at $12M the post-money is $84M and the plan funds about 200 robots, making a 2028 down round the base case [S95]; 2027 plan revenue at 10x is $56M, below the current mark [S95].",
   "outcome": "A 2030-2031 exit at about $100M: $12.0M to the lead, 1.1x before a 20% Series B dilution, 1.0x after.",
   "implication": "Return of capital at best; the position earns no venture return and should not be led."
  },
  {
   "case": "Bear",
   "probability": "42%",
   "driver": "The v4 misses $36,000, renewals stay near $12,700 or fall back toward $9,500, a second grower leaves over bruising, the licence falls non-exclusive below 100 robots on 2027-12-31, and the round closes at the $12M minimum or slips past the cash covenant.",
   "evidence": "Contribution is negative at every price up to $17,600 on the $48,000 build [S1]; Grower E left over bruising and Grower B cut from 22 robots to 14 [S1]; $2.2M of usable cash at $410,000 a month reaches the $1.5M floor around 2027-03-10 [S1]; 10% non-USMCA duty is $3,300 a robot, 85% of a season's gross profit [S89]; five of six capital-heavy peers sold assets or shut [S28, S93, S116].",
   "outcome": "A trade sale, asset sale or wind-down at $15-40M: $7.3M-12.0M to the lead, 0.6-1.0x, depending on where the $36.77M equal-rank preference falls short.",
   "implication": "Do not invest at $72M pre-money; the preference protects the downside only above about $25M of exit value, and the loss is a full return of capital at best."
