  "consensus": "The company and the $4.0M of insiders committing at the mark price Orrin as the only open-field strawberry harvester above 90% pick rate, on a 2.1-season payback, 52-61% gross margins at scale and $8M of ARR in 2027.",
  "our_view": "The thesis is consensus on the pain and non-consensus on everything that pays for it. The pain is real and independently measured; the price is not: one robot-season loses $8,100 after depreciation at the signed price, 44% of the $3.2M ARR is contracted rental, the company is not alone in the field, and $69.9M of enterprise value is 36.8x FY2025 revenue against a 2.3x peer median. We pass at $72M pre-money.",
